"match_fingerprint":"3d854bb62a0e60a14c6bf3f437729d9f8df71901939d42dac975db0b3823783d","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":86,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-39487d5e64bb43c4b1630e811a0a0b9f","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":100,"end_line":null},"finding":"references/doc_3934.md (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"- **如何实现高可用？** → [高可用](references/doc_3934.md)","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f1a6d06368ecf4db88e01875951198e4bae9cec59827c641204efd65849f56bf","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":100,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-39487d5e64bb43c4b1630e811a0a0b9f","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":303,"end_line":null},"finding":"references/doc_3934.md (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"- **如何实现高可用？** → [高可用](references/doc_3934.md)","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f1a6d06368ecf4db88e01875951198e4bae9cec59827c641204efd65849f56bf","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":303,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-73d3cca1c50e46edb10f1a862df5dd88","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3248.md","start_line":40,"end_line":43},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown explains that `forceDelete=true` will forcibly delete a partition even if it is currently being recovered. This is a safety-critical action that could impact data integrity or recovery state, but the document provides no explicit caution or warning to the user.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning that `forceDelete=true` should be used only in exceptional circumstances, may interfere with recovery operations, and can increase the risk of irreversible data loss or inconsistency.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3248.md","start_line":40,"end_line":43}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-03a494909f6e4aaba4b02902d3a7c357","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3592.md","start_line":64,"end_line":null},"finding":"chmod +x gui.sh\n./gui.sh\n若 GUI 无法启动，请在 GUI 安装目录下运行：\njava -version\n若系统不能显示 Java 版本信息，说明 Java 没有安装或 Java 的安装路径不在系统路径中。在 Windows 上，需要查看是否在\nPath\n中；在 Linux 上，需要查看是否在\nPATH\n中。\n若命令显示了 Java 版本信息，请检查版本是否符合要求。Do","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"DolphinDB GUI\n。安装前，需要确保已经安装 Java 8 及以上 64bit 版本。DolphinDB GUI 无需安装，开箱即用。在 Windows 环境下，双击 gui.bat 即可。在 Linu 和 Mac 环境下，在 Terminal 中输入：\ncd /your/gui/folder\nchmod +x gui.sh\n./gui.sh\n若 GUI 无法启动，请在 GUI 安装目录下运行：\njava -version","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2436d55a1bf73d976bc852d7f7c785c6b6ff9e3a48cdc5c4baa2a08f8b4a8a76","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3592.md","start_line":64,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-40bc5f0e25924b589c29d6254c45749c","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3592.md","start_line":64,"end_line":null},"finding":"chmod +x gui.sh\n./gui.sh\n若 GUI 无法启动,请在 GUI 安装目录下运行:\njava -version\n若系统不能显示 Java 版本信息,说明 Java 没有安装或 Java 的安装路径不在系统路径中。在 Windows 上,需要查看是否在\nPath\n中;在 Linux 上,需要查看是否在\nPATH\n中。\n若命令显示了 Java 版本信息,请检查版本是否符合要求。Do","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"DolphinDB GUI\n。安装前,需要确保已经安装 Java 8 及以上 64bit 版本。DolphinDB GUI 无需安装,开箱即用。在 Windows 环境下,双击 gui.bat 即可。在 Linu 和 Mac 环境下,在 Terminal 中输入:\ncd /your/gui/folder\nchmod +x gui.sh\n./gui.sh\n若 GUI 无法启动,请在 GUI 安装目录下运行:\njava -version","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse","normalized-view"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e1557a56e7e28727305a0111c3332d1463070b4fdbf6a32094a0bb8f751b49de","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3592.md","start_line":64,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-280a733a0e834d5aa9b51ab2932c8d16","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3592.md","start_line":193,"end_line":195},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown states that the default admin password is `123456` and provides direct login examples using those credentials, but does not clearly warn that leaving default credentials unchanged is unsafe except for a brief later note to change the password. Because this behavior affects account security and system integrity, the skill description should prominently disclose the risk and instruct users to rotate credentials before real use.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning the first time default credentials appear, stating they are for initial setup/demo only, must be changed immediately, and must never be used in production or exposed in shared dashboards/scripts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3592.md","start_line":193,"end_line":195}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c91fcaf8c0364983b4e5df6be6f19c75","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/doc_4723.md","start_line":39,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document states that the initial super administrator username is `admin` with password `123456`, and many later examples reuse those credentials, but there is no adjacent warning that these are default bootstrap credentials and must be changed before production use. Publishing default privileged credentials in operational guidance without a strong warning can lead users to deploy insecure configurations.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the default credential description and first login example that `admin/123456` is an initial default only for setup or demos, must be changed immediately, and must never be retained in production.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_4723.md","start_line":39,"end_line":40}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-c2d84de8c6af4b7696f650d8f9a296a3","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_539.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf /","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"system()\n函数返回值。\n例子\ncmd=\"rm -rf /home/user1/test.txt\"\nshell(cmd);","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f3ff4d6cfbe1b7f6b23dd4d1379edae984c14738c5f5b14db40e215beb673f08","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_539.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-792dccf32c82419297ff1f7c3a1cc9a8","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/doc_539.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf /home/user1/test.txt\"","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"system()\n函数返回值。\n例子\ncmd=\"rm -rf /home/user1/test.txt\"\nshell(cmd);","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"e950079df05a4aec80dba98b6681e10ee01b872c4abbbe811d59a3929a490b1a","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_539.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d5e9409709a64ab79002aa9d2c2f52cf","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":251,"end_line":258},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script removes directories with `rm -rf` and overwrites files via `cp -rpf`, affecting `/ddbdocker` paths on the host. While there is an interactive prompt in part of the script, the surrounding documentation lacks a clear upfront warning that running it can delete existing data or replace files.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning before the script block and before `sh map_dir.sh` stating that it may overwrite configuration/license files and delete existing data directories under `/ddbdocker`. Recommend backing up existing data and verifying target paths before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":251,"end_line":258}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-4bbbf45e3bc440dabc66bb4ac962984e","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":258,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf ./${ddb_name}","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"cp -rpf $source_dir4 $dir4\n\n#删除解压的安装包\nrm -rf ./${ddb_name}\n执行 shell 脚本，构建数据映射目录\nsh map_dir.sh && tree /ddbdocker\n期望输出：","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"0c9eeb17416aae7dc15d7f5e7c391feab043d5ea2d12abee87ca802bbd4263db","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":258,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f840acad2371444ebf251c97a5a1f6b4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5542.md","start_line":41,"end_line":43},"finding":null,"explanation":"The sample code conditionally executes `dropDatabase(dbName)`, which is a destructive and potentially irreversible operation affecting the entire database. The surrounding markdown does not provide a visible warning, caution note, or confirmation guidance for readers who may copy and run the example.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning before the example that it deletes the database if it exists, and recommend using a test database name, verifying the target, and backing up data before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5542.md","start_line":41,"end_line":43}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6e711434be1149d3a380f0008b3da4ca","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5856.md","start_line":176,"end_line":178},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example conditionally calls dropDatabase(\"dfs://db1\"), which is a destructive operation affecting stored data. In this markdown file there is no adjacent caution telling users the example deletes an existing database path if present.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning before the example that it deletes dfs://db1 if it exists, recommend using a temporary/test database name, and advise users to back up or avoid running it in production environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5856.md","start_line":176,"end_line":178}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-63e809f061c747c5acfa72f13b21140f","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":585,"end_line":null},"finding":"rm -rf .config/Code/Service\\","explanation":"Tool parameters are crafted to achieve unintended or unsafe behavior. Parameter abuse can bypass intended safety checks (e.g. shell=True, --force, dangerous glob patterns).","remediation":"Validate all tool parameters against an allowlist. Reject dangerous parameter values (shell=True, --force, -rf /) and use safe defaults.","code_snippet":"进程，并删除 service worker\n                                    缓存：\nlinux:\npkill code && rm -rf .config/Code/Service\\\n      Worker/{CacheStorage,ScriptCache}\nwindows:\n退出 vscode 之后，打开任务管理器，结束所有残留的 vscode 僵尸进程","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9596fa399cb1831067854b30beae836310bdb0af409172c6bbd0f7d41c09d5e6","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":585,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM2","finding_id":"finding-b424deee14e442b98765deb589dd98a0","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Chaining Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":585,"end_line":null},"finding":"&& rm -","explanation":"Tool calls are chained to bypass individual safety checks or escalate capabilities beyond what any single tool call would allow.","remediation":"Limit tool chaining depth and validate the output of each tool before passing it to the next. Require explicit user approval for multi-step chains.","code_snippet":"进程，并删除 service worker\n                                    缓存：\nlinux:\npkill code && rm -rf .config/Code/Service\\\n      Worker/{CacheStorage,ScriptCache}\nwindows:\n退出 vscode 之后，打开任务管理器，结束所有残留的 vscode 僵尸进程","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"da42bed49ba667f4edac8a3628fa28e5cc6bbc20fc757fb7d1ddbddd9a531ec0","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":585,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-88b575cd8f4d4e74bed61245e0c02c6a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":15,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"For a documentation skill whose stated purpose is technical reference and best practices, hardcoded admin/default-password login examples are not justified as a capability without strong warning or credential hygiene guidance. Repeating usable admin credentials normalizes insecure access patterns and can enable unsafe real-world use if copied verbatim.","remediation":"Remove default credentials from examples, replace them with placeholders, and add explicit guidance to use least-privilege accounts and rotate default passwords before any deployment.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":15,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"P2","finding_id":"finding-2251fc7a1cfa4e2cb55c95c9589e22c8","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Hid