ation":"Audit all comments and invisible characters. Remove any instructions that direct the agent to perform unauthorized actions. Use plain, reviewable content.","code_snippet":"为内存表，返回一个内存表，其行序与原表相反。\n若\nX\n为有序字典，返回一个有序字典，其键值对顺序与原字典​​相反​。\n例子\nreverse `hello `world;\n// output","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2d93fd660b4f174bc04f3ea25d6385f309664ddd20d9b629d066032c5d334a81","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":45,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P2","finding_id":"finding-2251fc7a1cfa4e2cb55c95c9589e22c8","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Hidden Instructions","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7657.md","start_line":26,"end_line":null},"finding":"​","explanation":"Hidden instructions were detected in comments or invisible text. These could contain malicious directives. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Audit all comments and invisible characters. Remove any instructions that direct the agent to perform unauthorized actions. Use plain, reviewable content.","code_snippet":"为内存表，返回一个内存表，其行序与原表相反。\n若\nX\n为有序字典，返回一个有序字典，其键值对顺序与原字典​​相反​。\n例子\nreverse `hello `world;\n// output","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2d93fd660b4f174bc04f3ea25d6385f309664ddd20d9b629d066032c5d334a81","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7657.md","start_line":26,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P2","finding_id":"finding-2251fc7a1cfa4e2cb55c95c9589e22c8","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Hidden Instructions","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":306,"end_line":null},"finding":"​","explanation":"Hidden instructions were detected in comments or invisible text. These could contain malicious directives. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Audit all comments and invisible characters. Remove any instructions that direct the agent to perform unauthorized actions. Use plain, reviewable content.","code_snippet":"为内存表，返回一个内存表，其行序与原表相反。\n若\nX\n为有序字典，返回一个有序字典，其键值对顺序与原字典​​相反​。\n例子\nreverse `hello `world;\n// output","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2d93fd660b4f174bc04f3ea25d6385f309664ddd20d9b629d066032c5d334a81","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":306,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a7d7b90585344e77974560bfa25f6a0a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7739.md","start_line":126,"end_line":133},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file shows a SQL Server IP address, username, and password directly in the example, then uses them in a connection string. For markdown files, SQP-2 applies when the skill description omits warnings about behaviors affecting privacy or sensitive data; exposing credential usage without a warning can normalize unsafe handling of secrets.","remediation":"Replace real-looking credentials with obvious placeholders, and add a warning that users should never hardcode or publish production credentials in documentation or scripts. Recommend secure secret storage methods such as environment variables or a secrets manager.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7739.md","start_line":126,"end_line":133}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d60484a1e8fd44b1aa63347f92ec5749","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7739.md","start_line":157,"end_line":162},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example connects to MySQL with a root account and plaintext password in the documentation. Because this is a markdown file, the missing-warning rule applies to documented behaviors that could affect privacy or system integrity, and no caution is provided here.","remediation":"Use non-sensitive placeholder values instead of real-style credentials and add a warning against embedding passwords in examples. Document safer alternatives such as prompting for credentials, environment variables, or external secret stores.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7739.md","start_line":157,"end_line":162}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-5f7a7a404f88438aab58b5595e69904c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":63,"end_line":63},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes a safety-sensitive operation: accessing an administrative interface using default credentials. While it explains how to log in, it does not provide any user warning about the security risk of leaving the default password unchanged, which could expose the cluster to unauthorized control.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the login instructions telling users that the default admin password is insecure and must be changed before exposing the service to other users or networks.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":63,"end_line":63}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0359841f392a414ea47416637276a5f8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":75,"end_line":77},"finding":null,"explanation":"The sample script checks for an existing database and calls dropDatabase(dbName), which is a destructive and potentially irreversible operation. The surrounding markdown presents this as setup code without any caution that running it against an existing environment will remove prior data.","remediation":"Add a clear warning before the snippet stating that dropDatabase will delete the target database and should only be run in a test environment or after confirming backups exist.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":75,"end_line":77}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0d9c3b11b7664780b82b068965de2ac2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":162,"end_line":162},"finding":null,"explanation":"This administrative login guidance uses well-known default credentials and omits any disclosure of the security implications. In documentation for a management interface, failing to warn about changing default credentials can lead users to deploy an insecure system.","remediation":"Add an explicit note that the default admin password is for initial setup only and must be changed before regular use or any network exposure.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":162,"end_line":162}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b4844e85b17c4158abe36fd5dc68b0fc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":176,"end_line":178},"finding":null,"explanation":"The snippet includes dropDatabase(dbName), which is a destructive database operation. The documentation does not disclose that executing this example on an existing instance will remove the current database contents.","remediation":"Insert a warning before the code block explaining that dropDatabase is destructive and should only be used on disposable test data or after backup/confirmation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":176,"end_line":178}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-5a7dfe6b37c243b3bdb08e8c78ae5d26","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":289,"end_line":305},"finding":null,"explanation":"The embedded DolphinDB script templates include explicit admin logins with static passwords and then perform destructive operations such as dropping partitions and dropping tables before rewriting data. For a skill whose stated purpose is broad technical documentation, embedding privileged administrative credentials and destructive maintenance examples is an unjustified capability escalation relative to normal reference usage.","remediation":"Remove hard-coded admin credentials from examples and replace them with placeholders plus least-privilege guidance. Separate destructive administrative procedures into a clearly marked advanced/admin-only section, or omit them from the skill if such capability is outside the intended scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":289,"end_line":305}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-96cce26a06ae4bc0a47f5e639722e17a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":83,"end_line":88},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document describes configuring `publicName` for external access to the cluster Web management interface and later for data and compute node Web interfaces, but does not warn that these interfaces provide administrative and interactive access. For a markdown skill, omission of a clear warning about privacy and system-integrity impact when exposing management endpoints is a safety issue.","remediation":"Add explicit warnings wherever `publicName` is introduced that exposing these interfaces to the Internet can allow unauthorized management or data access unless protected by strong credentials, network restrictions, TLS, and other access controls.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":83,"end_line":88}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b082e029d5244e87b756df6377536270","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":519,"end_line":519},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document instructs users to log into the Web management interface with the default admin account and password (`admin` / `123456`) as part of cluster operation. Because this interface controls starting, stopping, and managing cluster nodes, the skill should explicitly warn users that these defaults are insecure and must be changed before any real deployment or external exposure.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near the first login instructions stating that the default credentials are for initial setup only, must be rotated immediately, and should never be exposed on public networks. If possible, include steps for changing the admin password before continuing.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":519,"end_line":519}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-340ca5613bb947bf80c3856cfff0d21a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":936,"end_line":938},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document advises solving Web access problems by closing the firewall on the server or opening the required ports, but does not clearly warn that disabling a firewall broadens network exposure and can endanger cluster management and data services. This omission is material because the same guide also documents externally reachable management interfaces and default credentials.","remediation":"Replace the recommendation to disable the firewall with safer guidance to open only required ports from trusted sources, and add an explicit warning against broadly disabling host firewalls on production or Internet-reachable systems.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":936,"end_line":938}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-eec3edf57ef24c5b93d3f89e8e6704a4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/doc_914.md","start_line":141,"end_line":143},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example explicitly drops the existing OHLC table before recreating it, which is a destructive and potentially irreversible operation. The surrounding markdown explains the mechanics but does not provide a caution that existing data will be deleted.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning that db.dropTable(\"OHLC\") deletes the existing table and its contents. Recommend backing up data, using a non-production database, or renaming the output table to avoid accidental loss.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_914.md","start_line":141,"end_line":143}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f422221253b34df9915b7c73c06bba05","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":516,"end_line":522},"finding":null,"explanation":"The function is documented as deleting all shared tables, a destructive operation that can affect user data and active workflows, yet no explicit caution or data-loss warning is provided. Markdown descriptions should clearly warn users when behavior can remove data or disrupt system state.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning that `clearAllSharedTables()` deletes all shared tables on the current node, may cause data loss or service disruption, and should be used only after backups or confirmation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":516,"end_line":522}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6ba6dfd59e8042a0a2b2e92df660982d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":530,"end_line":539},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description says the function clears the entire stream environment, including subscriptions, engines, and shared tables, but does not include an explicit high-visibility warning about service interruption or possible data loss. Given the broad and destructive scope, the markdown should disclose this impact clearly.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning that `clearAllStreamEnv()` performs multiple destructive cleanup actions, may interrupt streaming services and remove shared tables, and should only be run during controlled maintenance.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":530,"end_line":539}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-94c39674144a44759958d33f488b6cce","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":628,"end_line":631},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file states that all persistent stream tables are deleted, but no explicit warning is provided about irreversible deletion or the impact on stored data. For markdown documentation, destructive operations affecting persisted data require clear user-facing warnings.","remediation":"Add a prominent caution that `clearAllPersistenceTables()` deletes all persistent stream tables and may permanently remove data unless backups or recovery plans are in place.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":628,"end_line":631}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f787a313c8aa4a7f87a13303631acf68","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9483.md","start_line":270,"end_line":270},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown explicitly tells users to log in with the default account 'admin' and password '123456' for cluster management. This is a safety-sensitive administrative access path, but the document provides no warning that these default credentials must be changed immediately or that leaving them in place risks unauthorized access.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning next to the default credential instructions stating they are for initial setup only and must be rotated before exposing the interface or using the cluster in any shared environment. Include steps for changing the admin password and recommend restricting network access until credentials are updated.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9483.md","start_line":270,"end_line":270}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f7a79593ff454bb98f0800f1e7dd8b6f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9483.md","start_line":704,"end_line":704},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown advises users they can solve web management access issues by closing the firewall on the server hosting DolphinDB. Disabling a firewall affects system integrity and exposure, yet the document does not warn users about the risk or prefer safer alternatives such as opening only required ports from trusted sources.","remediation":"Replace the firewall-disabling advice with a least-privilege recommendation to allow only the necessary management ports from approved IP ranges. If firewall disablement is mentioned at all, mark it as a temporary troubleshooting step with a strong warning about increased attack surface.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9483.md","start_line":704,"end_line":704}]},{"id":"P6","finding_id":"finding-8377558d1f49479cb0945512b15cae55","category":"System Prompt Leakage","pattern":"Direct Prompt Extraction","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/whitepapers/streaming.md","start_line":2075,"end_line":null},"finding":"return rule","explanation":"Skill contains instructions that could directly expose system prompts, internal rules, or hidden instructions to users or external parties.","remediation":"Remove any instructions that reveal, print, or output system prompts or internal rules. System instructions should never be exposed to end users.","code_snippet":"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tamount>LARGE_AMOUNT)\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn rule1 or rule2\n\n\\}\n","intent":null,"tags":["System Prompt Leakage"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"457bb74dd0eb3f195d54fbf3bf07e26dc6f982b06ad90b9a248f56071c83b964","occurrences":[{"file":"references/whitepapers/streaming.md","start_line":2075,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8a64eabb2e564ca69423d560eff2bd34","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":183,"end_line":185},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes example commands that unsubscribe a stream handler and drop a stream engine, which can disrupt running workflows or remove active processing state. The surrounding documentation does not warn users that these commands modify or tear down existing runtime objects before execution.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the example stating that the cleanup commands stop/remove existing subscriptions and engines, and should only be run in a test environment or after confirming the target objects are safe to delete.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":183,"end_line":185}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bd638b8e1ea94cde8c649ce53ed2cbaa","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":191,"end_line":191},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example instructs users to load a shared library plugin from a filesystem path, which executes externally provided code inside the database environment. The markdown does not disclose that only trusted plugins should be loaded or that plugin execution can affect system integrity.","remediation":"Add a warning that shared-library plugins execute native code, should come only from trusted sources, and may require validation or sandboxing before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":191,"end_line":191}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-c68eef3095894cbdbc3476b0678d13cd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"metadata.json","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The top-level description is entirely in Chinese and presents the skill as Chinese-language documentation, but the metadata does not indicate that this is an optional locale variant or a region-specific skill. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in or justification is a natural-language policy concern.","remediation":"Clarify that this is a Chinese-language variant of the skill, add explicit locale metadata or user opt-in for Chinese content, or document why the skill is intentionally limited to Chinese users/content.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"metadata.json","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-767d846c48cf4123a991dd5155f00fdd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_104.md","start_line":13,"end_line":24},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents a command that deletes one or more chunk replicas and includes an example deleting all chunk replicas on a node. The description does not warn about data availability, recovery implications, or the need for operator caution, which is a missing user warning for destructive behavior in markdown documentation.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the description and example stating that this operation is destructive, may affect redundancy or availability, should be performed only after verification/backup, and should be used with caution in production.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_104.md","start_line":13,"end_line":24}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-da2940498e824b99ab213a203d8a7a94","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1062.md","start_line":13,"end_line":24},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents a cache-clearing operation that removes multiple kinds of cached data, including map-reduce intermediate results, but provides no cautionary note about operational impact. For markdown files, behaviors that can affect system integrity or active data processing should include an explicit warning to users.","remediation":"Add a warning section stating that `clearAllCache()` clears in-memory caches and distributed computation intermediate results, may affect active queries/jobs and performance, and should be used only when the user understands those impacts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1062.md","start_line":13,"end_line":24}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-ff3b7ba94b1f4bfc91ce8a7f57119250","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1083.md","start_line":3,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document is presented entirely in Chinese and points to a Chinese-language documentation source, with no indication that language selection is optional. Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language policy violation unless the locale constraint is clearly documented and justified.","remediation":"Add an explicit note that the skill/documentation is Chinese-language by design and justified for a China-specific audience, or provide a language choice / alternate localized version for users.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1083.md","start_line":3,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-43924b37cebd45108f5efeb234c6cc7a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1296.md","start_line":13,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents a destructive operation: deleting a cross-process shared memory table. Although it states that shutdown does not remove the table and that this function does, it does not provide an explicit warning about data loss or advise users to verify the target before deletion.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description stating that the operation permanently removes the specified shared memory table, may cause data loss or affect other processes using it, and should be used only after confirming the table name and impact.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1296.md","start_line":13,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-921d56bc71574611aad0ba402ee793ba","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_157.md","start_line":13,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains how to load DolphinDB plugins and focuses on login, permissions, and purchase requirements, but it does not warn that plugins include binary files (.dll/.so) that execute code and can affect system integrity. For a skill description involving plugin loading, a user-facing warning about trusting plugin sources and the risks of loading untrusted plugins is expected.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description or examples stating that loading plugins executes external binary code, should only be done for trusted plugins from verified sources, and may affect system stability or security.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_157.md","start_line":13,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-14b3cf9ff36a4dd8967bd953c757d29e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/doc_157.md","start_line":85,"end_line":87},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown example shows a connection string containing a username and password, but the surrounding documentation does not warn users not to hardcode or expose real credentials. Because the example demonstrates handling sensitive authentication data, the skill description should include a privacy and secret-management warning.","remediation":"Add guidance ליד the example to avoid hardcoding real usernames or passwords, use secure secret storage or environment-based configuration, and sanitize examples so they do not normalize unsafe credential handling.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_157.md","start_line":85,"end_line":87}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0ba8917c3b094ea79495916bbdce4d6a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1625.md","start_line":132,"end_line":132},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes an example that calls dropDatabase(dbPath), which is a destructive operation that can permanently remove data. The surrounding documentation does not provide any warning, confirmation note, or caution that the example deletes an existing database if present.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the example stating that dropDatabase deletes the target database and should only be run in a test environment. Consider revising the sample to use an isolated temporary database name and explicitly label the step as destructive.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1625.md","start_line":132,"end_line":132}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bdf6f82c690a4f0f81ada7a34d8ad227","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1706.md","start_line":119,"end_line":120},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes example code that checks for an existing database and drops it, which is a destructive operation affecting stored data. The surrounding documentation does not warn users that running the example will delete the database if it exists.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the example stating that `dropDatabase(\"dfs://rangedb\")` deletes existing data, and recommend using a test database path or removing the deletion step unless the user intends to reset the environment.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1706.md","start_line":119,"end_line":120}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-64263d20afaf440a8a19763f2f420e9e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1710.md","start_line":55,"end_line":56},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file instructs users to '关闭防火墙或者打开对应的部署端口' to access the web management interface, but it does not warn that disabling a firewall can reduce host and network security. Because the guidance affects system integrity and network exposure, the skill description should include a clear caution and safer preference.","remediation":"Add a warning that disabling the firewall increases attack surface and should be avoided unless necessary. Prefer instructing users to open only the specific required port, restrict source IPs where possible, and re-enable protections after troubleshooting.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1710.md","start_line":55,"end_line":56}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4d6d569947bf4d06ab9e0b1a39c04268","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1710.md","start_line":251,"end_line":252},"finding":null,"explanation":"The FAQ recommends resolving access issues by closing the firewall or opening the deployment port, but it omits any warning about the security consequences of disabling firewall protections. For markdown files, behaviors that could affect system integrity should be accompanied by explicit user warnings.","remediation":"Revise the FAQ to warn users that disabling a firewall weakens system security. Recommend opening only the needed port, limiting network exposure, and using temporary, documented exceptions instead of fully disabling the firewall.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1710.md","start_line":251,"end_line":252}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-43c48fa959934c2492eb342f34f8608b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1761.md","start_line":62,"end_line":114},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes example output showing fields such as userID, clientIP, and clientPort, along with concrete sample values, but it does not warn readers that the function reveals potentially sensitive user and network metadata. For markdown files, SQP-2 applies when the description omits warnings about behaviors that could affect privacy or expose sensitive system information.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the return-value description or examples stating that getJobStatus exposes job metadata including user IDs, client IPs, and ports, and that users should restrict access and avoid sharing output containing sensitive operational details.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1761.md","start_line":62,"end_line":114}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d8b8bbb781e5413db46753902a38a8f7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1810.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document states that scripts or functions are transmitted to a remote database for execution, which can affect remote systems and transmit local data. The page provides usage details and examples but does not include any warning about trust boundaries, side effects, or executing only trusted code on trusted hosts.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the description or examples that remoteRun executes code on a remote server and may transmit scripts and arguments over the connection. Advise users to use trusted endpoints, review transmitted data, and understand the impact of running remote code before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1810.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8f64e59180404d83b6e05dce216d19f1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1921.md","start_line":37,"end_line":41},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes example commands that create a directory and write data to disk using mkdir, saveText, and database creation/loading paths. The description does not warn users that running the example will modify the local filesystem, which is a user-impacting operation covered by the markdown warning requirement.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the examples stating that the commands create local directories and write files under C:/DolphinDB/Data, and advise users to adjust the path or use a safe test environment before running them.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1921.md","start_line":37,"end_line":41}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2c1e482b819a4e61a7a9fa9ce266bafa","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_1968.md","start_line":13,"end_line":19},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document states that the function overwrites a trading calendar file in memory and synchronizes the change to `marketHolidayDir`, but it does not include a caution about modifying system calendar data or the operational impact of changing trading-day logic. Because this is a markdown file describing a potentially integrity-affecting operation, an explicit warning is expected.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description stating that this operation changes trading calendar data in memory and on disk, may affect scheduling/calculation behavior, and should be used only after verification and with appropriate backup/change-control procedures.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_1968.md","start_line":13,"end_line":19}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f4de5809fc7849499c5fb0760faa723a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2146.md","start_line":15,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that the sql function dynamically generates SQL and that eval executes the generated statement, but it does not include any user warning about the risks of executing dynamically constructed queries. Because the examples later show user-influenced parameters being incorporated into generated queries, the omission reduces user awareness of potential data-access or unintended-query impacts.","remediation":"Add a short warning near the function description stating that dynamically generated SQL should only be built from trusted or validated inputs, and that eval will execute the generated statement against the target data source.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2146.md","start_line":15,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8aca2d92daaf477e88b7defc9bf73f70","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_223.md","start_line":142,"end_line":145},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains an example that logs in as admin and conditionally drops a database. Although the code is illustrative, the surrounding documentation does not visibly warn readers that running the snippet can delete existing data, which is a user-data integrity risk.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the example stating that it deletes the `dfs://replaceColumn` database if it exists, and advise users to run it only in a test environment or after changing the database path.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_223.md","start_line":142,"end_line":145}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-d9b2085d41594e1898bbd3725c15377f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2237.md","start_line":13,"end_line":24},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes this skill as a collection of DolphinDB technical documentation and white papers, implying an informational/read-only scope. This file documents `writeLog`, a function whose purpose is to write entries into a log file after login, which is a state-changing operation rather than documentation-only behavior.","remediation":"Clarify in the manifest that the skill includes documentation for administrative and state-changing database functions, or narrow the included content to read-only/reference materials if the intended scope is purely informational.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2237.md","start_line":13,"end_line":24}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-be27dc35ce8446889ae1685ec2c37262","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2274.md","start_line":375,"end_line":421},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents that locally defined functions can be serialized to remote nodes with the current user's privileges, and later shows creating a user account remotely. Those behaviors can materially affect system integrity and access control, but the surrounding description does not include a clear warning or caution to users before presenting the commands.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the RPC/remoteRun examples that remote execution runs with the caller's privileges and can modify remote systems, including user/account state. Recommend using least-privilege accounts, restricted environments, and confirming authorization before running the examples.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2274.md","start_line":375,"end_line":421}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6f7307790bc5455ca9b6149344d0f922","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2321.md","start_line":20,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents a safety-relevant behavior change to distributed database writes, including allowing concurrent writes to the same partition and the possibility that some partitions succeed while others fail. Under the markdown warning criteria, it should clearly caution users about data integrity and operational impact before or alongside the usage guidance.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the parameter description or example stating that using CHUNK may weaken transactional guarantees, can cause partial writes across partitions, and may slow writes due to retries; advise users to use it only when they accept those tradeoffs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2321.md","start_line":20,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e66e127255584bbcbed8b7ce22bb6f0a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2337.md","start_line":433,"end_line":502},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file describes enabling query logs, audit logs, and raw script logs that record user IDs, session IDs, query details, login/logout events, permission changes, and users' original script contents. Although the behavior is documented functionally, there is no explicit warning to users or operators about the privacy and sensitive-data implications of collecting and retaining this data.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the logging sections that enabling these options may capture sensitive user activity, script contents, identifiers, and security events, and should be enabled only with appropriate notice, retention controls, and access restrictions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2337.md","start_line":433,"end_line":502}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6fd0c6e60d6f4a4a9ecdc87dca7b61f8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2337.md","start_line":1853,"end_line":1857},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file instructs users to configure `s3AccessKeyId` and `s3SecretAccessKey` for AWS S3 access, but it does not warn that these values are sensitive credentials that must be protected from disclosure. For documentation that affects user data and system security, omission of a credential-handling warning is a meaningful safety gap.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning that S3 access keys are secrets, should not be committed to source control or shared in logs, and should preferably be supplied via secure secret-management mechanisms with least-privilege IAM settings.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2337.md","start_line":1853,"end_line":1857}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f8b995fc467341de88fc846591219bac","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2449.md","start_line":13,"end_line":28},"finding":null,"explanation":"This is a markdown file, so SQP-2 applies to omissions of warnings about behaviors that could affect system integrity. The text explains that the command modifies reserved memory online and gives parameter constraints, but it does not explicitly warn users about operational risks such as degraded performance, memory pressure, or disruption if misconfigured.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning stating that changing reserved memory is an administrative, system-impacting operation that may affect stability, performance, or availability, and should be performed carefully during controlled maintenance or after validating memory limits.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2449.md","start_line":13,"end_line":28}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c727cad0c6c6465cb217bb634e6d761d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"loca