n existing database and then calls `dropDatabase(dbName)` to remove it, but the documentation does not disclose that this is destructive. Readers following the example could delete a real database unintentionally because no caution or safe-testing guidance is provided.","remediation":"Add a visible caution before this example explaining that `dropDatabase(dbName)` permanently deletes the target database. Suggest using a non-production test name and requiring readers to verify the target before executing the snippet.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2829.md","start_line":198,"end_line":199}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f6244d32b4be4bb192c91c0c5afe6549","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2877.md","start_line":16,"end_line":16},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file states that `nullFill!` modifies the input object in place, which can affect user data or system state. Under the markdown-specific warning criterion, the description should explicitly warn users about the risk of unintended data mutation rather than only describing behavior tersely.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description, such as noting that `nullFill!` mutates the original object and should be used carefully or only on data the user is prepared to modify.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2877.md","start_line":16,"end_line":16}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d8300450a9274e5a80d9f3ca08699147","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2977.md","start_line":77,"end_line":77},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes a concrete credential value for first login: admin/123456. Because the file is a markdown document, SQP-2 applies when user-impacting or security-relevant behavior lacks warning; here, the text does not warn that the default password is insecure or should be changed immediately after setup.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the first-login instructions that the default admin password is for initial setup only and must be changed immediately before any non-test use or network exposure.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2977.md","start_line":77,"end_line":77}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-5eb70cc23fe5425898e4704b02d57971","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_2979.md","start_line":29,"end_line":30},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains an example that conditionally deletes a database via `dropDatabase(\"dfs://valuedb\")`, which is a destructive operation affecting user data. The surrounding documentation does not warn that the example will remove an existing database before proceeding.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the example stating that it deletes the existing `dfs://valuedb` database if present, and recommend running it only in a test environment or after confirming the data can be safely removed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_2979.md","start_line":29,"end_line":30}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-5315a6f742f241cf8808b2a158eb4bd0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3003.md","start_line":55,"end_line":72},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file instructs users to run privileged `sudo sysctl` commands and edit `/etc/sysctl.conf`, which changes kernel networking settings on the host system. The section provides operational steps but does not include any warning that these are privileged, system-wide changes that m