handling and storage security. Although it mentions that an empty keyPath means no encryption, it does not provide any user-facing warning about the privacy/integrity implications of writing backups or leaving them unencrypted.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning in the documentation that backupTable writes data to the filesystem, may create sensitive backup copies, and that omitting keyPath leaves backups unencrypted. Recommend choosing a secure destination, protecting access permissions, and enabling encryption when appropriate.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3236.md","start_line":13,"end_line":29}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c365ea6aa4f24d8ea68c1c6667d312d6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3236.md","start_line":42,"end_line":44},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example code conditionally calls dropDatabase(dbName), which is an irreversible destructive operation. In this markdown documentation, there is no warning telling users that running the example may delete an existing database with the same name.","remediation":"Add a clear caution near the example stating that it deletes an existing database if present, and advise users to run it only in a test environment or after changing dbName to a disposable path.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3236.md","start_line":42,"end_line":44}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a0b74221bc594b3aa3cef1602c6919fd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3248.md","start_line":17,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `dropPartition` as deleting partition data, including examples that remove database partitions and optionally schema metadata. While the behavior is described functionally, it does not clearly warn users that these operations are destructive and may permanently remove data across one table or all tables in the database.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the description and examples stating that `dropPartition` permanently deletes partition data, may affect all tables when `tableName` is omitted, and should be used only after confirming backups or recovery plans.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3248.md","start_line":17,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-450d74376ed941ddb4a4e1043dc8c312","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3248.md","start_line":44,"end_line":55},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file states that `deleteSchema=true` can delete both partition data and the corresponding partition schema information when certain conditions are met. Although the behavior is described, there is no explicit caution highlighting that this removes metadata in addition to data and may complicate restoration or future operations.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning that enabling `deleteSchema` removes partition metadata as well as data, describe the operational consequences, and recommend confirming intent or ensuring recoverability before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3248.md","start_line":44,"end_line":55}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8e2ab7464be64ae08fff3a962deaa0c6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3404.md","start_line":21,"end_line":23},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `overwrite=true` as deleting users and function views not present in the backup, which can materially affect system integrity and access control. Although the behavior is described, it is not presented as a clear warning or caution to the user about the destructive nature of the operation.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning/caution near the `overwrite` parameter and examples stating that `overwrite=true` will delete existing users, permissions, and function views not present in the backup and should be used only after verifying the backup and target environment.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3404.md","start_line":21,"end_line":23}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0a2011bb79a54c52b2cd278c41f4eace","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3475.md","start_line":55,"end_line":56},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes executable example code that opens a session to a remote host and sends a command, but the surrounding documentation does not warn readers that running the sample will contact an external server. For markdown files, behaviors that affect privacy or system/network integrity should be disclosed to the user.","remediation":"Add a clear note near the example stating that it connects to an external DolphinDB server and transmits authentication/session data, and advise users to replace the host with their own trusted test environment before running it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3475.md","start_line":55,"end_line":56}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8b0b8d9ded0e4bbaa786ab773834abbe","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3475.md","start_line":136,"end_line":136},"finding":null,"explanation":"The sample shows a literal password value inside a login example, but the markdown does not warn users that this is placeholder/demo data and that real credentials should not be embedded in scripts. In documentation for authentication behavior, omission of such warning can mislead users into unsafe handling of sensitive data.","remediation":"Label the password as dummy data and add guidance to load credentials securely from protected input or environment variables instead of hardcoding them.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3475.md","start_line":136,"end_line":136}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-85d863be952447d5ad1b53b906d724af","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3503.md","start_line":21,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file instructs the user to manually copy database-related directories and then delete the originals, which is a safety-critical operation affecting user data and system integrity. Although the procedure includes operational steps, it does not explicitly warn about the risk of irreversible data loss if the copy or path change is incomplete or incorrect.","remediation":"Add a clear warning before the migration steps stating that copying and deleting these directories is destructive and can cause permanent data loss or service outage if done incorrectly. Recommend verifying backups, confirming copy integrity, and ensuring the server is stopped before deleting the source directories.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3503.md","start_line":21,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6b61c1d3966a49acbcc8af518282f6ec","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3525.md","start_line":13,"end_line":31},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that the function creates a file containing all configuration information, including license, machine core count, memory information, and cluster configuration details. Because this behavior can expose sensitive system and environment data, the skill description should explicitly warn users before presenting or recommending its use.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description stating that the generated bundle may include sensitive configuration, licensing, topology, and system information, and should only be shared with authorized parties after review.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3525.md","start_line":13,"end_line":31}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-10423688446e4abca60815278a05ba66","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3544.md","start_line":59,"end_line":60},"finding":null,"explanation":"L059-L060 说明 outputSt1 用于“满足第一个需求的跟踪状态变化的输出表”，而后续代码却在 L093-L094 将响应式状态引擎绑定到 outputSt2。类似地，L070-L071 说明 outputSt2 用于告警输出，但 L109-L110 又将会话窗口引擎绑定到 outputSt1，属于文档说明与代码行为的直接矛盾。","remediation":"统一文档与示例代码中的输出表命名和绑定关系。要么将响应式状态引擎输出改为 outputSt1、会话窗口引擎输出改为 outputSt2，要么修正文档对两个表用途的描述，确保定义、创建和验证部分一致。 ","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3544.md","start_line":59,"end_line":60}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8ec66175be88436e8bde401079374874","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3576.md","start_line":45,"end_line":50},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes an example function that cancels all unfinished jobs across the cluster via `getRecentJobs`, `cancelJob(jobids)`, and `pnodeRun`, but it does not warn users that this can interrupt other users' running work or cause loss of in-progress computation. For markdown files, omission of warnings about behaviors affecting system integrity or user work qualifies as a missing user warning.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the example stating that cancelling jobs is disruptive, may terminate other users' unfinished batch jobs, and should only be used by authorized administrators after confirming impact.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3576.md","start_line":45,"end_line":50}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-6892a5cfe14c4a688f1e54a7fe33cc4b","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.65,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3592.md","start_line":41,"end_line":null},"finding":"nohup ","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"上述命令中采用前台运行的方式，若要后台运行，修改\n./dolphindb\n命令为\nnohup ./dolphindb -console 0 &\n或\nsh startSingle.sh\n，然后用命令","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"a3b2c30e52b72d9ed99fed84c020ce072453b04697f4f184c9268de970914edb","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3592.md","start_line":41,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-6892a5cfe14c4a688f1e54a7fe33cc4b","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.65,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":827,"end_line":null},"finding":"nohup ","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"上述命令中