lete data and should be used cautiously, especially outside test environments.","remediation":"Add a visible caution before the examples stating that they perform destructive actions, should only be run in test environments unless intended, and may permanently remove table contents or databases.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_4815.md","start_line":98,"end_line":129}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c1941be6aea740128f8a7bf468cbde87","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"references/doc_4871.md","start_line":14,"end_line":25},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown explains that append! directly modifies the target object and later shows appending into distributed tables, which can affect stored data. Although there are technical notes about column order and partition constraints, there is no explicit warning framing the operation as a potentially data-altering action users should use cautiously.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near the introduction stating that append! performs in-place mutation and can permanently alter vectors, tables, or distributed tables. Include guidance to verify schema/order and consider backing up or testing on a copy before running against important datasets.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_4871.md","start_line":14,"end_line":25}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-080f81e167ef43ef8e1fffcfdf72a21a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_4898.md","start_line":63,"end_line":72},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents actions that write streaming data to disk and instructs users to terminate the server with `kill -15`, while noting that crashes or `flushMode=0` may cause data loss. Under the markdown-specific warning rule, behaviour affecting user data and system integrity should be clearly surfaced as a warning, and the current note is technical guidance rather than an explicit safety warning.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning section stating that enabling persistence writes data to disk, server termination affects availability, and asynchronous or non-sync flush modes can lead to data loss. Place the warning near the command overview and examples so users see it before applying the operation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_4898.md","start_line":63,"end_line":72}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c440c875fc664c49b8fe9a0dd46ee9a6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_4942.md","start_line":13,"end_line":30},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file describes clearing memory and disk caches on compute nodes, including wildcard and all-partition targeting, but it provides no warning about operational impact or the broad scope of the action. Because this behavior can affect system performance and data availability characteristics, the description should disclose the risk before showing usage examples.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that the command clears node memory and disk caches, may impact running workloads or performance, and can apply broadly when table or partition is omitted or wildcarded. Include guidance to confirm the target database/tables/partitions before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_4942.md","start_line":13,"end_line":30}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b1b65f0ef9d14c99bddb32efc4f2f1db","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_4983.md","start_line":17,"end_line":19},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents a destructive operation that can delete non-empty directories when `recursive=true`, but it does not include any explicit warning about irreversible data loss or impact on user data. Under the markdown-specific missing-warning rule, destructive behavior affecting filesystem contents should be clearly disclosed.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near the description of `recursive=true` stating that it permanently deletes the target directory and all contained files/subdirectories, and advise users to verify the path before running it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_4983.md","start_line":17,"end_line":19}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a5809c0e8a9e4c608763d5bfb1a5e368","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5013.md","start_line":248,"end_line":249},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown explains that restore operations will overwrite partitions whose timestamps differ and delete partitions that exist in the target database but not in the backup. These are destructive data-affecting behaviors, but the surrounding examples and instructions do not present a prominent safety warning or explicit caution before running the restore commands.","remediation":"Add a clear warning adjacent to the restore examples stating that restore may overwrite target data and remove partitions absent from the backup. Recommend restoring into a new database first or verifying the target path before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5013.md","start_line":248,"end_line":249}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-846860c322e441fab5f3e794485857b0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5013.md","start_line":336,"end_line":336},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document states that for migrate, original databases and tables must already be deleted or recovery cannot proceed. Because this implies destructive preconditions affecting user data, the section should include an explicit warning to back up and verify deletion targets before proceeding.","remediation":"Add a conspicuous warning in the migration section that existing databases/tables may need to be deleted and that users should confirm backups and target names before running migration.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5013.md","start_line":336,"end_line":336}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-969aca9fb2ee4c45ae23dfc84ca4b11f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_503.md","start_line":37,"end_line":43},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that data outside the retention window is deleted and suggests using `dropPartition` to remove older data, but it does not clearly warn users that these actions are destructive and may permanently remove stored data. For markdown files, operations affecting user data or system integrity should include an explicit warning.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the retention/deletion description and the `dropPartition` reference stating that retention settings and partition deletion can permanently remove data, and advise users to verify backups or confirm the policy before applying it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_503.md","start_line":37,"end_line":43}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bfd93d8b141d4a01993fd7a00eb443f5","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5055.md","start_line":13,"end_line":19},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents an operation that starts data or compute nodes in a cluster, which can affect system availability and infrastructure state. The description and example show how to perform the action but provide no warning about operational impact, required privileges, or the need to verify the target nodes before execution.","remediation":"Add a brief warning that startDataNode changes live cluster state, should be run only by authorized operators on intended nodes, and may affect running workloads or system behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5055.md","start_line":13,"end_line":19}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-312f8b6d1a53424dadd82f67cdf27c73","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5125.md","start_line":456,"end_line":537},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes operational examples that write to /home/root/WORK_DIR, create snapshot directories, persist shared tables, and submit a continuously running job. The surrounding documentation presents these actions as example steps but does not include any caution about filesystem changes, persistence side effects, or the need to stop the infinite writer process.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the example explaining that it writes to local disk, enables persistent shared tables, and launches a continuous job that consumes resources until stopped. Recommend using a test environment and adjusting paths/cleanup steps before running.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5125.md","start_line":456,"end_line":537}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-287273782b17417c980b4090e517da89","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5126.md","start_line":130,"end_line":133},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document shows `login(\"admin\", \"123456\")` and notes that this is the initial administrator account, but it does not explicitly warn users to change default credentials or avoid using them in production. Because administrator credentials affect system integrity, the documentation should include a clear safety warning.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning that `admin/123456` is a default example credential, should be changed immediately, and must not be used in production or exposed in shared environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5126.md","start_line":130,"end_line":133}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a18b491d709341ecb0ee69f2e767b58d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":34,"end_line":40},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document includes commands to disable ufw and later stop and disable firewalld, but it does not clearly warn that doing so reduces host security and should only be done in controlled environments. Omitting that warning can lead users to weaken system protections without understanding the risk.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that disabling the firewall exposes the host to network risk and should only be done temporarily or in trusted environments. Prefer documenting least-privilege port-opening as the safer default.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":34,"end_line":40}]},{"id":"PE2","finding_id":"finding-a962effb8ba54a729aa4e258b4451dc4","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Sudo/Root Execution","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3003.md","start_line":56,"end_line":null},"finding":"sudo ","explanation":"Commands invoke sudo or root privileges. Verify this elevated access is necessary and justified.","remediation":"Avoid sudo/root unless strictly required. Prefer least-privilege patterns. If elevation is needed, document the justification and scope.","code_snippet":"若使用 Ubuntu 系统，注意以下几点：\n需要在系统安装时在 Storage configuration 中选择 /home 目录的格式为 xfs，以方便后续将 /home 目录格式化为 xfs 文件系统；\nUbuntu 系统使用 ufw 防火墙，关闭防火墙命令为\nsudo ufw disable\n，其他命令请参考\nman ufw\n；","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"16746f7044f347c6322d4c5b879b3fb06b2f205cbf1c9a209b43d52b34b3afd7","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3003.md","start_line":56,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE2","finding_id":"finding-a962effb8ba54a729aa4e258b4451dc4","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Sudo/Root Execution","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3003.md","start_line":57,"end_line":null},"finding":"sudo ","explanation":"Commands invoke sudo or root privileges. Verify this elevated access is necessary and justified.","remediation":"Avoid sudo/root unless strictly required. Prefer least-privilege patterns. If elevation is needed, document the justification and scope.","code_snippet":"若使用 Ubuntu 系统，注意以下几点：\n需要在系统安装时在 Storage configuration 中选择 /home 目录的格式为 xfs，以方便后续将 /home 目录格式化为 xfs 文件系统；\nUbuntu 系统使用 ufw 防火墙，关闭防火墙命令为\nsudo ufw disable\n，其他命令请参考\nman ufw\n；","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"16746f7044f347c6322d4c5b879b3fb06b2f205cbf1c9a209b43d52b34b3afd7","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_3003.md","start_line":57,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"PE2","finding_id":"finding-a962effb8ba54a729aa4e258b4451dc4","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Sudo/Root Execution","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/doc_3003.md","start_line":58,"end_line":null},"finding":"sudo ","explanation":"Commands invoke sudo or root privileges. Verify this elevated access is necessary and justified.","remediation":"Avoid sudo/root unless strictly required. Prefer least-privilege patterns. If elevation is needed, document 