],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"16746f7044f347c6322d4c5b879b3fb06b2f205cbf1c9a209b43d52b34b3afd7","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9483.md","start_line":757,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-3caafa9fc3454275a7f7451975ad086a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":78,"end_line":99},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section instructs the user to reformat /home, remove a logical volume, and restore data, which can cause permanent data loss or system disruption if performed incorrectly. Although it includes steps, it does not provide an explicit warning highlighting the destructive and potentially irreversible nature of the operation.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning before these steps stating that unmounting /home, removing the logical volume, and reformatting will disrupt the system and may permanently destroy data if backups are incomplete or commands are misapplied. Recommend verifying backups and maintenance windows before proceeding.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":78,"end_line":99}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f285848b30a94b31ab473aba65f27994","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":193,"end_line":200},"finding":null,"explanation":"The instructions configure unlimited core dumps for all users and write crash files to disk, but they do not warn that core dumps may contain sensitive application memory, credentials, or personal data. This is a privacy and security-relevant behavior that should be disclosed in the documentation.","remediation":"Add a warning that core dumps can contain sensitive in-memory data and should be enabled only when needed, with restricted filesystem permissions and retention controls. Consider scoping the setting to the DolphinDB user rather than all users.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":193,"end_line":200}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-3bd0bbd3aed443018732f9f5938fdfa2","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":305,"end_line":null},"finding":"systemctl enable","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"# server 3.centos.pool.ntp.org iburst\n...\n分别在两台虚拟机上启动 ntpd\n# systemctl enable ntpd\n# systemctl restart ntpd\n等待若干秒后，查看 ntpd 运行状况\n虚拟机1：","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9bd3987b1e7eb1f3ae4e81621a2f94408559610e4556fdb1373fa6f662c9f677","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":305,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-3bd0bbd3aed443018732f9f5938fdfa2","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":927,"end_line":null},"finding":"systemctl enable","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"# server 3.centos.pool.ntp.org iburst\n...\n分别在两台虚拟机上启动 ntpd\n# systemctl enable 