ing firewalld reduces network security and should only be used when compensating controls exist. Emphasize opening only required DolphinDB ports instead of disabling the firewall entirely.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5216.md","start_line":318,"end_line":326}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4b22cb915c2649029977cb57c941c4d2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5241.md","start_line":36,"end_line":38},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes executable example code that checks for an existing database and deletes it via `dropDatabase(db_name)`. The surrounding documentation does not warn users that running the example can permanently remove existing data, which is a missing user warning for a destructive operation in markdown content.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the example stating that it deletes an existing database and may cause data loss. Prefer using a disposable test database name in the example and explicitly instruct users not to run it against production data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5241.md","start_line":36,"end_line":38}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-438a70e470a7483db624360afcdaf104","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_527.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown describes that the function stops persistence and deletes the table contents on disk while retaining only the table structure. This is a destructive operation affecting stored data, but the document provides no warning, caution note, or explicit disclosure about data loss risk.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description stating that this operation deletes persisted table contents from disk and may cause irreversible data loss. Include guidance on backups, intended use cases, and confirmation precautions before running it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_527.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-0cf3dc5edff446ef965b77ef80b06a7c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_539.md","start_line":13,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes the skill as providing DolphinDB technical documentation and best practices. This file documents a `shell(cmd)` capability that executes OS commands, a powerful host-level action that is not inherently aligned with a documentation-focused skill purpose and could enable command execution guidance beyond the stated scope.","remediation":"Constrain the skill corpus to documentation directly relevant to database usage, or explicitly declare that administrative/system-command documentation is in scope. If retained, clearly label such content as privileged administrator-only functionality and restrict agent use of it to documentation-only responses.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_539.md","start_line":13,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1d647a227c22455fb9eb431b6b5107f9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_539.md","start_line":25,"end_line":26},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes an example using `rm -rf` to delete a file via the `shell` function, but it provides no warning that the example performs destructive filesystem modification. For markdown files, safety-impacting behaviors that can affect user data or system integrity should be accompanied by a clear warning or caution.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the example stating that `shell(cmd)` can execute destructive OS commands and that `rm -rf` deletes data irreversibly. Consider replacing the example with a harmless command or clearly marking it as a dangerous administrative example.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_539.md","start_line":25,"end_line":26}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-d5c761aae5a94203b0deb0bfedb53cfc","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Docker image references without a specific tag (:latest is implicit) or digest (@sha256:...) can be silently replaced by a malicious image.","remediation":"Pin the image: image:tag or image@sha256:abc123","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"34cb2682080126d49b307c03f0efd8eb332e2a00cabbee958db5e3bf3beba89d","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":20,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-081678ebbad74f238eda6f44d4a7469e","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":34,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Docker image references without a specific tag (:latest is implicit) or digest (@sha256:...) can be silently replaced by a malicious image.","remediation":"Pin the image: image:tag or image@sha256:abc123","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b06f2d75e46984d3a97dd8e091874992b2602d3f1e43afdc641e20fde0d2eac0","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":34,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-081678ebbad74f238eda6f44d4a7469e","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","sta