hanges. The section does not include an explicit warning that this runs external code and may modify local directories and files.","remediation":"Add a warning before these commands that the script is executed on the host and will create/modify directories and files. Recommend reviewing the script contents before execution and running it with appropriate permissions in a controlled environment.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":96,"end_line":99}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-5686d6a9d64241e384edf7a528a2a82b","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":346,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Docker image references without a specific tag (:latest is implicit) or digest (@sha256:...) can be silently replaced by a malicious image.","remediation":"Pin the image: image:tag or image@sha256:abc123","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8ad028f5723e2e55c646e9ae2f13a94f83d35d7ad12d81f1a61a37853b9e9f41","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":346,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-6260ae3e10414011a08944165e691093","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":392,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"Docker image references without a specific tag (:latest is implicit) or digest (@sha256:...) can be silently replaced by a malicious image.","remediation":"Pin the image: image:tag or image@sha256:abc123","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"a4d22f8956eeee37219813aeefbe887006e5aa2ac272ca58a9ddc2877dfe795f","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5479.md","start_line":392,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9c92b35957cc4a1da16269596b863343","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5542.md","start_line":13,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that `truncate` deletes all data from a distributed table and also recommends `dropTable` when the table structure need not be preserved. It presents irreversible data-destruction behavior as normal usage, but does not include an explicit warning or caution to users about permanent data loss or safe-use considerations.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near the function description and examples stating that `truncate`, `dropTable`, and related commands irreversibly delete data and should only be run on the intended database/table after verification or backup.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5542.md","start_line":13,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ecfd411274c64bf0a8d3daa61656fb39","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5642.md","start_line":99,"end_line":99},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains an example login command using explicit credentials (`login('admin', '123456')`). The surrounding documentation does not warn users not to use default credentials or to substitute their own secure values, which is a missing user warning for a security-relevant operation.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the example stating that the credentials are illustrative only, must be replaced with environment-specific secure credentials, and default/admin passwords should never be used in production.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5642.md","start_line":99,"end_line":99}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e787c2c7d7a643b38f636c509f31fc17","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5643.md","start_line":50,"end_line":58},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file describes a function that returns potentially sensitive session information, including user IDs, client IP addresses, ports, and activity timestamps. Under the markdown-file warning criteria, the description omits any warning that using or sharing this output may affect user privacy or expose system/session metadata.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the return-value section stating that the function exposes session and client metadata (for example user IDs, remote IPs, ports, and activity times) and should be used only by authorized users and handled carefully in logs, screenshots, or shared outputs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5643.md","start_line":50,"end_line":58}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-18758aaf9ebc46cdb452d2646170eed3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5643.md","start_line":102,"end_line":108},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example shows a concrete user entry with session ID, memory usage, remote IP, remote port, and timestamps, which could normalize disclosure of operational metadata. The surrounding markdown does not warn readers to sanitize or avoid exposing such data when using examples or sharing command output.","remediation":"Add a note before the example indicating that returned records may contain sensitive operational and user metadata, and redact or anonymize example values such as user IDs, IP addresses, ports, and timestamps.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5643.md","start_line":102,"end_line":108}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b07765decaff4e99828aa93e6ee04951","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5651.md","start_line":13,"end_line":38},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file describes extracting query logs from saved distributed table access records, including fields such as userid and script, which may expose sensitive user activity and SQL contents. The description states the function is admin-only, but it does not warn readers about privacy or audit sensitivity when accessing or handling these records.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that the function retrieves sensitive audit data, including usernames and SQL text, and should only be used for legitimate administrative or compliance purposes with appropriate access controls and data-handling precautions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5651.md","start_line":13,"end_line":38}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-56c17416aa84423cbe7273ca386bf5f0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/doc_5672.md","start_line":14,"end_line":29},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents a database table restore capability, which can affect user data and system integrity, but it does not explicitly warn users about restore risks such as overwriting target tables, restoring into the wrong database, or requiring validation before use. Although it includes technical constraints, those are not framed as user-facing safety warnings.","remediation":"Add a clear warning section stating that restoreTable can modify database state and should be used only after verifying the backup source, target database/table, engine and partition compatibility, and any overwrite or replacement consequences.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_5672.md","start_line":14,"end_line":29}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding