ps a database if it exists, which is a destructive operation affecting user data and system state. The surrounding documentation provides no warning, confirmation note, or caution that running the example can delete data.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the example stating that `dropDB` deletes the database and should only be run in a disposable test environment. Consider renaming the sample database more explicitly as a test-only resource and noting that users should avoid running it against real data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_595.md","start_line":90,"end_line":90}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-83ead0f0425545c4b8970eed53e6824b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_6055.md","start_line":14,"end_line":21},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents saving strings to a file by appending or overwriting existing content, which can affect user data and system integrity. While it explains the append parameter semantically, it does not explicitly warn users that using overwrite mode may replace existing file contents and cause irreversible data loss.","remediation":"Add a clear warning in the description or parameter section stating that the function writes to the filesystem and that append=false will overwrite existing file contents. Include a brief caution to verify the target path and mode before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_6055.md","start_line":14,"end_line":21}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2eb83f65e5fc42269c142d4707a254b9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_6069.md","start_line":13,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `dropDistributedInMemoryTable`, which deletes a specified table, but the description and return-value section provide no caution about destructive impact, potential data loss, or the need to verify the target before execution. Under the markdown-specific SQP-2 criteria, destructive behavior that could affect user data should include an explicit warning.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description and example stating that the command permanently removes the specified distributed in-memory table, may cause data loss, and should be used only after confirming the target table and operational context.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_6069.md","start_line":13,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-66eaa4f8d5a14cb2962941303105d079","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_6104.md","start_line":117,"end_line":121},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes example code where the callback uses append! to write rows into a distributed table, which is a persistent data-modifying operation. The surrounding documentation describes the behavior functionally but does not provide any caution or user-facing warning about the side effect on stored data.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the callback example stating that the sample writes data into the distributed table dfs://temp/pt and modifies persistent storage. Mention that users should review the destination table and adapt the callback before running in real environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_6104.md","start_line":117,"end_line":121}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b77402e7b28a4f20bf1922d4a0d0f4aa","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/doc_6182.md","start_line":192,"end_line":192},"finding":nu