md","start_line":384,"end_line":385}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-92253148aebb461c92dc537e713123f6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_6767.md","start_line":421,"end_line":422},"finding":null,"explanation":"This example removes an existing database before creating a new one, but the document does not alert readers that the operation is destructive. The lack of warning is material because users may copy and run the sample directly.","remediation":"Document that dropDatabase permanently deletes the database, and advise users to confirm the target and avoid production environments when running the example.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_6767.md","start_line":421,"end_line":422}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f68a7e93889f4f6fa323349c08cf8220","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_680.md","start_line":68,"end_line":69},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown documents that when snapshot=true, deleted source tables or partitions will also be deleted from the backup, which is a destructive behavior affecting backup integrity. Although the behavior is explained, there is no explicit warning or caution callout highlighting the risk of data loss to users.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near the snapshot parameter and examples stating that enabling snapshot=true can remove tables or partitions from existing backups and may cause irreversible loss of backup contents if used unintentionally.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_680.md","start_line":68,"end_line":69}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-32c6aa782cbd4e8196e5f1075320faa4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"references/doc_680.md","start_line":176,"end_line":198},"finding":null,"explanation":"The examples show db.dropPartition operations and demonstrate that subsequent backup behavior can preserve or remove deleted partitions, affecting recoverability. The documentation lacks a clear caution that these examples involve destructive deletion and can change what data remains restorable from backups.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning before the examples noting that dropPartition is destructive and that backup/restore results differ materially depending on snapshot settings, potentially removing recoverable data from backups.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_680.md","start_line":176,"end_line":198}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b0e0275053e441a98d9fecd2e43ed34f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_6890.md","start_line":13,"end_line":16},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that scripts or functions are transmitted to and executed on a remote database, which can affect remote systems and execute arbitrary code. The description provides no warning about verifying trust, permissions, or potential impact of running remote code.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the overview or examples stating that remoteRunCompatible executes code on a remote database, should only be used with trusted endpoints/scripts, and may affect remote data or system state.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_6890.md","start_line":13,"end_line":16}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-97ced982566843229b250342c8b3ffeb","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_6970.md","start_line":31,"end_line":32},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes examples that drop a database and later drop a table column, but the document provides no warning that these actions can delete data or irreversibly change schema. For markdown files, safety-impacting behaviors should be disclosed to users when the description or examples could affect user data or system integrity.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the examples stating that `dropDatabase` deletes the database and that `alter table ... drop` irreversibly removes a column/data; recommend testing on non-production data and backing up before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_6970.md","start_line":31,"end_line":32}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e4ee186888d2467aa1cf9200e3e6ebe8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/doc_6970.md","start_line":98,"end_line":98},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example explicitly demonstrates `alter table pt drop value` without any cautionary note about permanent schema and data loss. In markdown documentation, destructive operations should be accompanied by warnings so users understand the risk before copying the command.","remediation":"Add an inline note or warning before the example explaining that dropping a column is irreversible, may delete stored values in that column, and should only be run after confirmation/backup.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_6970.md","start_line":98,"end_line":98}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4a32d6b6bb914c86b1c3f06e77c6d4d6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7063.md","start_line":50,"end_line":52},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes sample code that conditionally calls `dropDatabase(dbName)`, which is a destructive operation affecting user data/system integrity. The surrounding documentation does not include any warning, caution note, or disclosure that the example deletes an existing database.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the example stating that it will delete the specified database if it exists, and recommend using a test database name or removing the destructive lines before running in non-test environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7063.md","start_line":50,"end_line":52}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9c5e9213e6f341e385d7f177ebdb3b6c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7159.md","start_line":14,"end_line":21},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents an operation that writes a backup containing user information, permission data, and function views to disk. Because the description does not warn that the output file is sensitive and should be protected, users may underestimate the privacy and security impact of creating or storing the backup.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description and fileName parameter stating that the backup contains sensitive user and permission data, should be written only to secure locations with restricted access, and should be handled carefully during storage and transfer.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7159.md","start_line":14,"end_line":21}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-7251e36769774cf2900c059fc1a99aea","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7191.md","start_line":214,"end_line":216},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file instructs users to use `loadTextEx` to write imported data directly into a distributed database, which can modify persistent storage. The document explains efficiency benefits but does not include any warning or caution about overwriting, appending, or otherwise affecting stored data.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the first `loadTextEx` usage that the operation writes data directly to the database and may alter persistent data, and recommend verifying the target database/table before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7191.md","start_line":214,"end_line":216}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2f84d09a2a1b4a9d9f92880b827d8919","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7196.md","start_line":22,"end_line":23},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents behavior that can affect user access and system session integrity, including logging out all sessions on data, compute, and control nodes and allowing administrators to log out other users. The description explains the behavior but does not include any explicit caution or warning about its disruptive impact.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the function description or examples stating that setting sessionOnly=false or using the function as an administrator can terminate active sessions across the cluster and disrupt other users, and recommend verifying intent before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7196.md","start_line":22,"end_line":23}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-cca5db32480046ed9679dbb67d8d398f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7228.md","start_line":42,"end_line":45},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file shows an example script that logs in with explicit credentials and drops a database, but the surrounding documentation does not warn readers that the example performs destructive operations and uses sensitive authentication data. For markdown files, examples that could affect user data or system integrity should include clear warnings.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the example stating that it contains login credentials and deletes the database `dfs://tedb`, and clarify that users should not run it unchanged in production or against real data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7228.md","start_line":42,"end_line":45}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-744bae05461a4422a033f51a9c735bc8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7235.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents an administrative operation that modifies the memory cap for batch subquery results on the current node. The description states what the command does, but provides no caution about possible effects such as query failures, performance degradation, or instability from misconfiguration.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the command description stating that changing the memory limit can affect running queries and node stability, and that administrators should verify the value carefully before applying it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7235.md","start_line":13,"end_line":13}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-068bc6b2842f47aaa4d95d30ceba8589","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7284.md","start_line":43,"end_line":52},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains executable sample code that connects to DolphinDB using explicit admin credentials and a plaintext password. Although the file demonstrates a networked database operation, it does not warn readers that the credentials are examples only or that secrets should be externalized, which could lead to unsafe copy-paste use.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the sample code stating that the username/password are placeholders for local testing only and should not be hardcoded in real deployments. Prefer environment variables, secret managers, or interactive credential input in the examples.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7284.md","start_line":43,"end_line":52}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-12183647752b4193bfe6aa13a383160b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7284.md","start_line":129,"end_line":135},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown includes a step that runs dropStreamTable on a named table, which is a destructive operation affecting system state. While the step label says it deletes the table, there is no explicit caution or warning to users about data loss or advising them to verify the target before running it.","remediation":"Add a warning before the deletion example that this command removes the specified stream table and may delete data/state. Recommend using a test environment, verifying the table name, and avoiding execution against production instances unless intended.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7284.md","start_line":129,"end_line":135}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a2d70ef874e04da681489124a0038ab4","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7284.md","start_line":182,"end_line":205},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section again provides ready-to-run connection and writer initialization examples with admin credentials and a plaintext password. The document does not disclose the risks of embedding credentials in code or instruct users to replace them with secure secret-handling mechanisms.","remediation":"Add an explicit note that the credentials are illustrative only and should not be committed or reused in production. Replace hardcoded secrets in examples with environment-variable lookups or placeholders like <DB_PASSWORD>.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7284.md","start_line":182,"end_line":205}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-684f31d23fab4330b5f4fe3ae299b824","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7284.md","start_line":892,"end_line":902},"finding":null,"explanation":"The appendix repeats a directly executable connection example using admin and a plaintext password, which may encourage insecure reuse. The markdown does not include a warning that secrets should be managed securely and not embedded in source or documentation.","remediation":"Annotate the appendix example with a warning that credentials are test placeholders only. Update the sample to read credentials from environment variables or clearly mark them as values the user must substitute securely.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7284.md","start_line":892,"end_line":902}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b4637be4f16b4dcdb6d98284dc190084","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7286.md","start_line":20,"end_line":21},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents modes such as \"w\" and \"w+\" that will truncate an existing file or create a new one, which can affect user data. The description explains behavior but does not include any cautionary warning about data loss or the irreversible nature of clearing a file.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the mode descriptions and/or examples stating that \"w\" and \"w+\" will overwrite or clear existing files and should be used carefully.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7286.md","start_line":20,"end_line":21}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6c09f7423a7e4cf9aaf2456722311520","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":239,"end_line":315},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file instructs users how to upload files from VS Code to a DolphinDB server, including automatic path mappings to remote destinations. Because this operation transmits user files to a server and may affect data privacy, the skill description should include a clear warning about verifying file contents and remote target paths before upload.","remediation":"Add a brief warning in the upload section stating that uploading sends local files to the configured server, may expose sensitive data, and that users should confirm the selected file and remote destination before proceeding.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":239,"end_line":315}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-127920333c334d52a8ccadf6ef071cc0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":316,"end_line":320},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown explains how to export database table data to a chosen local path, but it does not warn users that the exported file may contain sensitive database contents or affect existing files at the destination. For a data-writing operation, a user-facing warning in the documentation is expected when privacy or data integrity could be impacted.","remediation":"Add a warning that exported data is written to local disk, may contain sensitive information, and users should choose a safe destination and avoid overwriting important files.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7287.md","start_line":316,"end_line":320}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8277f9e66fe147998e0e17217e0db1fd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7416.md","start_line":13,"end_line":16},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents an operation that deletes a file, but it does not include any explicit caution or warning about potential data loss beyond stating that login is required. For markdown files, destructive behaviors that can affect user data should be accompanied by a clear warning.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the description or syntax stating that `rm` permanently deletes the specified file and should be used carefully, ideally with guidance to verify the path before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7416.md","start_line":13,"end_line":16}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-489c0323cfd84c47ae76c85fc95e9129","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7520.md","start_line":362,"end_line":367},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document tells users to replace the existing `marketHoliday` folder on servers and, for online updates, to not keep the original folder. These are potentially disruptive file-system changes that can affect system integrity, but the description does not provide a clear user-facing warning about backup, rollback, or service impact beyond procedural notes.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning before these steps stating that replacing or removing the existing `marketHoliday` folder can overwrite current data, disrupt service until restart/update completes, and should only be done after backup and during a maintenance window.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7520.md","start_line":362,"end_line":367}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d8ad7ded96cc44ad840334134888e012","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7520.md","start_line":368,"end_line":392},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section provides code that calls `updateMarketHoliday` and `addMarketHoliday`, and notes it can be propagated to other nodes with `pnodeRun`. Although consistency limitations are mentioned, the markdown does not clearly warn users that the operation modifies calendar files/state across the cluster and may cause partial or unintended changes if misapplied.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that the script performs cluster-affecting updates, should be tested in a non-production environment first, and requires backups and coordinated rollout/rollback procedures.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7520.md","start_line":368,"end_line":392}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c12e72acd307488e827d4b9739e195f9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7533.md","start_line":14,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that the function enables automatic cache cleanup for non-persistent stream tables and that older published records are purged from memory once thresholds are reached. Because this behavior deletes data from memory, the skill description should include an explicit user warning about potential data loss or retention impact.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description stating that enabling this feature automatically removes older in-memory records based on size or time thresholds, and advise users to confirm retention settings before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7533.md","start_line":14,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-082c8c373f034210be14b978a9aaf60e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":15,"end_line":19},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest claims the skill provides '最佳实践' (best practices), but the example immediately instructs use of the default admin account and default password. That directly conflicts with secure best-practice intent because default privileged credentials should not be recommended for routine examples without an explicit warning.","remediation":"Revise examples to use non-privileged placeholder accounts and add a note that default admin credentials are for initial setup only and must be changed before normal use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":15,"end_line":19}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f2a331cb2c374cb8b462be38fd53a12a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":15,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file shows logging in with the default username and password (`admin` / `123456`) as part of example setup, but does not warn readers that these are insecure defaults and should not be used in real environments. Because the file is markdown and describes authentication-related behavior that can affect system integrity, it should include an explicit warning or note to change credentials.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the first login example stating that `admin` / `123456` are default demo credentials only, must be changed before any non-demo use, and should never be exposed in production or shared environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":15,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-89c9f65600844a5da6645e20f191c478","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":26,"end_line":32},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes the skill as a collection of technical documents and best practices, which implies reference/documentation scope. This file contains concrete commands to create distributed databases and partitioned tables, and later also appends data and drops databases/tables, which goes beyond passive documentation content into operational write/destructive behavior examples.","remediation":"Clarify in the manifest that the skill includes executable admin/write examples for DolphinDB, or segregate operational/destructive examples from read-only reference materials and label them prominently as write-capable demonstrations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":26,"end_line":32}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4392bd4fd4654135a7f22cc52f6661da","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":446,"end_line":454},"finding":null,"explanation":"Multiple markdown examples connect to DolphinDB using hard-coded `admin` / `123456` credentials, but the document does not caution users against copying this pattern into real deployments. This omission weakens user awareness around credential safety and may encourage insecure operational practices.","remediation":"Add a repeated or global note that these credentials are for local demo purposes only, recommend storing credentials securely, and show a safer pattern such as prompting for credentials or reading them from protected configuration.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":446,"end_line":454}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bd446b205ccd4aa38e4dc55693f94581","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":455,"end_line":457},"finding":null,"explanation":"The markdown embeds code that checks for an existing database and then calls `s.dropDatabase(dbPath)`, which is a destructive operation. The surrounding text does not clearly warn users that running this example may delete an existing database and its contents.","remediation":"Add a visible warning immediately before this example explaining that it deletes the target database if it already exists, and advise readers to use a disposable test database name or remove the deletion call before running in any environment with valuable data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7605.md","start_line":455,"end_line":457}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c52e4ccf92ab4b0f93ddb21eb5479033","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_761.md","start_line":304,"end_line":315},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file instructs users to run unsubscribeTable, dropStreamEngine, and dropStreamTable to tear down a streaming environment. Although it describes what the commands do, it does not warn that these actions can stop active processing and remove in-memory resources, which may affect running workloads or data availability.","remediation":"Add a clear warning before the cleanup section stating that these commands are destructive or service-impacting, should only be run intentionally, and may interrupt active jobs or remove in-memory tables/engine state. Recommend verifying the target environment and active subscriptions before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_761.md","start_line":304,"end_line":315}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bd849e1a674e47e7b0a57ca5b23fbb8e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7615.md","start_line":83,"end_line":85},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes example commands that delete original databases via `dropDatabase(\"dfs://db1\")` and `dropDatabase(\"dfs://db2\")`. Although the examples are part of a migration workflow, the surrounding text does not explicitly warn readers that these commands are destructive and can permanently remove existing data.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the example stating that `dropDatabase` permanently deletes databases and should only be run intentionally, preferably after verifying backups or in a test environment.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7615.md","start_line":83,"end_line":85}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8c51be38bf6d49fbaa8188fa6dfdcb09","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7628.md","start_line":13,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents an operation that removes previously published MCP tools, which can affect system availability or user workflows. The description provides syntax and an example but does not include any caution, confirmation note, or warning about the consequences of revoking a published tool.","remediation":"Add a clear warning in the documentation stating that `withdrawMCPTools` revokes published tools and may disrupt dependent workflows. Include guidance to verify the target tool names and confirm intent before running the command.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7628.md","start_line":13,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e7d07eb7f25d4995b88698c89e6a2987","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7642.md","start_line":146,"end_line":150},"finding":null,"explanation":"This is a markdown file, so SQP-2 applies to omissions in user-facing warnings. The examples show direct use of credentials such as \"123456\" and \"abcdec\" in login/createUser commands, but the document does not warn readers not to use real credentials, avoid plaintext handling, or prefer safer practices in production.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the examples stating that the passwords are placeholders for demonstration only, should not be reused in real environments, and that credentials should be handled securely according to deployment best practices.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7642.md","start_line":146,"end_line":150}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-e5f58041c1fc495293cf61375e3a3c62","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7793.md","start_line":13,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents a restore-like action: loading backup data into a specified partition of a distributed table. Although it notes that login is required, it does not warn users that the operation may alter database state or impact existing data, which is a user-safety concern for markdown files describing system-affecting behavior.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description and example stating that loadBackup performs a data restore/load operation that can affect database contents, should be used only with intended backup data, and should be verified in a non-production or backed-up environment before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7793.md","start_line":13,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b7ce675797734501a289917fe023def7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7820.md","start_line":28,"end_line":30},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown documents fetching plugin binaries and description files from a remote repository using plain HTTP, which can affect system integrity by installing executable components. The description does not include any warning about trusting the source, verifying integrity, or the risks of downloading and loading remote binaries.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that installPlugin downloads executable plugin files from a remote server and may affect system integrity. Recommend using trusted repositories, verifying plugin integrity/authenticity, and noting any network or installation side effects before users run the command.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7820.md","start_line":28,"end_line":30}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-08554fee3c7049d8a2fa55c6f5a14b25","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7821.md","start_line":16,"end_line":18},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents that `winsorize!` changes the input object in place, which can affect user data integrity. Although the behavior is mentioned, there is no explicit cautionary warning or highlighted notice to alert users to the destructive nature of mutating the original object.","remediation":"Add a clear warning section stating that `winsorize!` mutates the input object `X` in place and may overwrite existing data. Recommend using the non-mutating `winsorize` variant when users want to preserve the original input.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7821.md","start_line":16,"end_line":18}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-84148ceb33b543369d999a8494fcc024","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":66,"end_line":66},"finding":null,"explanation":"Changing firewall settings affects system security and can expose administrative services to unintended networks. The document treats this as a connectivity step without warning users to restrict access, use specific allow-rules, or avoid exposing the management interface publicly.","remediation":"Add a warning that firewall changes may expose the management interface and recommend allowing only required ports from trusted hosts instead of broadly disabling the firewall.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":66,"end_line":66}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2ad6e1ca3189401fad2061131993029c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":165,"end_line":165},"finding":null,"explanation":"Firewall configuration changes are safety-relevant because they can expose management services to broader network access. The document omits a caution about limiting exposure to trusted networks or preferring narrow inbound rules over disabling the firewall.","remediation":"Add a warning explaining the risks of disabling the firewall and recommend opening only necessary ports for trusted source addresses.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_7984.md","start_line":165,"end_line":165}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-25748b14046e429b915a0c6477d236d3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8009.md","start_line":45,"end_line":134},"finding":null,"explanation":"该 markdown 文件介绍了文本/二进制文件导出、数据库写入以及 AWS S3、HDFS、消息中间件等读写能力，可能影响用户数据、外部系统或网络边界。但文档整体仅陈述功能，没有提醒覆盖写入、数据同步、网络传输或实时写入可能带来的风险。","remediation":"在相关段落补充明确警告，说明这些功能可能执行文件覆盖、数据库落盘、外部系统写入或网络数据传输；建议提示用户在生产环境操作前确认目标路径、目标库、凭据来源及覆盖/同步影响。","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8009.md","start_line":45,"end_line":134}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-c81a24a4084f476094c1134b1634d047","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":1,"end_line":426},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest frames the skill as a documentation/best-practices corpus, but this document goes beyond passive reference material by providing executable configuration and script content for importing data into DolphinDB. It explicitly documents write-side behaviors such as append, update, dropPartition, dropTable, and scheduled sync workflows, which are materially more operational than a purely descriptive documentation scope suggests.","remediation":"Clarify in the manifest that the skill includes operational runbooks and executable import/synchronization examples for DolphinDB, including write/update workflows. If the intended scope is truly reference-only, exclude or clearly segregate documents containing executable administrative and data-modification procedures.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":1,"end_line":426}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-3604e597ef994ac48d9caec293c35c85","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":19,"end_line":23},"finding":null,"explanation":"The surrounding prose presents the plugin as a data import/sync tool, but the included template code implements updates by extracting full-table data, deleting partitions, dropping tables, and rewriting data. That is more invasive than a typical reader would infer from '导入' or '同步', creating an intent-level mismatch between the documentation framing and the actual scripted behavior.","remediation":"Revise the documentation to explicitly state near the introductory description that some update modes are implemented through destructive rebuild operations, including partition or table replacement. Add prominent warnings about side effects, required privileges, and rollback limitations before the template code.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":19,"end_line":23}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-54401b7cd97c4c93ba3acafb4310a296","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":22,"end_line":23},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that updates are implemented by extracting full-table data, deleting partitions, and rewriting them, and also notes the operation is not atomic. However, it does not provide an explicit safety warning to users about possible data loss, inconsistency, or failed-update recovery steps before they follow the procedure.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near this section stating that the process deletes and rewrites data partitions, is non-atomic, and may cause inconsistency or data loss on failure. Recommend backups, maintenance windows, and validation before use in production.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":22,"end_line":23}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-10b40a7cf3a44fe98d3faf363fcf4873","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":96,"end_line":131},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section instructs users to implement scheduled synchronization via shell scripts, Python, cron, and local JSON state files, adding automation and persistent state management capabilities beyond simple reference content. While relevant to a deployment workflow, these capabilities are broader than what the manifest's high-level description of technical documentation alone communicates.","remediation":"Update the manifest to state that the skill includes deployment and automation runbooks, including scheduled sync scripts and local state management. Otherwise, narrow the included content to conceptual documentation and non-operational examples.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8011.md","start_line":96,"end_line":131}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9557e221d52745a2a1c676bcd6db2a82","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8103.md","start_line":351,"end_line":378},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `update` operations that rewrite entire tables or partitions (`update pt set x=x+1`, `update pt set value = 1`) and also shows `dropDatabase(dbName)`. Although the page is technical documentation, it does not include a clear caution that these examples modify stored data and may irreversibly affect a user's database if run as-is.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the example sections stating that the commands mutate database contents and may delete data, and advise users to run them only in a test environment or after backing up data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8103.md","start_line":351,"end_line":378}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f3cf2259fbde40c6b185ee502f72ae0c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8110.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation states that clip! modifies the input object X in place, which can affect user data by changing existing state. The markdown does not provide any caution or warning language to alert users to this destructive side effect.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the syntax or details section stating that clip! mutates the input object X in place and may overwrite existing values, and advise users to copy data first if they need to preserve the original.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8110.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-12bcc42bcd9a471abfa5734b7e2c640a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8161.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `dropColumns!` as deleting specified columns from a table, which can affect user data and system integrity. The description presents the operation plainly without any warning or caution that it mutates the table and may irreversibly remove data.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the description and examples stating that `dropColumns!` mutates the table by removing columns and may cause irreversible data loss; recommend backing up data or confirming intent before use.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8161.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4aa6d30ce8ff41169f6f43d5fccc10af","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8238.md","start_line":21,"end_line":30},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `script` as code or a function name to be executed remotely and returns the execution result, but it provides no user-facing warning about the risks of remote execution. Because markdown files should warn about behaviors that could affect user data or system integrity, the omission is notable here.","remediation":"Add a brief warning that `remoteRunWithCompression` executes code on a remote database/server, may affect remote data or system state, and should only be used with trusted scripts and intended targets.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8238.md","start_line":21,"end_line":30}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-5a6c3fbe226b48769fadc74f85368fcf","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8239.md","start_line":13,"end_line":14},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file states that `dropDatabase` deletes all physical files of the specified database and also removes catalog references, but it does not provide an explicit warning or caution to users about the irreversible impact. Because this is a markdown documentation file describing a destructive operation, the absence of a prominent warning about potential data loss matches the missing user warnings criterion.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description and examples stating that `dropDatabase` permanently deletes database files and related catalog references, may cause irreversible data loss, and should only be used after confirming backups or user intent.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8239.md","start_line":13,"end_line":14}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0f3022b8c7f84679bd0c927ed73ca244","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":529,"end_line":531},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example instructs users to drop an existing database if it exists before recreating it, which can permanently delete prior contents of `dfs://testDB`. In markdown documentation, destructive behaviors affecting user data should be accompanied by a clear warning so users do not run sample code against real environments unintentionally.","remediation":"Add a caution before the sample code stating that `dropDatabase(dbName)` permanently deletes the existing database and should only be used in a disposable test environment or after confirming backups.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8250.md","start_line":529,"end_line":531}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-993df6bec4b344a3b0ab48c464b20e99","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8252.md","start_line":3,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file points to a Chinese-language documentation URL and labels the source in Chinese, while the entire skill content is presented only in Chinese. Under the policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a natural-language policy concern unless the locale restriction is explicitly justified.","remediation":"State that this skill is intended specifically for Chinese-language DolphinDB documentation, or provide an explicit language choice / alternate localized versions so users are not forced into a single language unexpectedly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8252.md","start_line":3,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-fff7bd99172d442380942f7b7f914073","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_836.md","start_line":13,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that `setDynamicConfig` modifies system configuration online, which can affect system behavior and availability, but it provides no cautionary warning, confirmation note, or guidance about using it carefully in production. Because markdown files should warn about actions that may affect system integrity, the omission qualifies as a missing user warning.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the description and examples stating that changing runtime configuration can impact performance, stability, or connectivity, and recommend verifying values and using the command only with appropriate administrative review, especially in production environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_836.md","start_line":13,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-a7658989d5dd4a0f89afa17f485ad35f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8454.md","start_line":280,"end_line":281},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes an example that checks for an existing database and then deletes it with `dropDB(\"dfs://test\")`. The surrounding documentation does not warn that the example removes an existing database path and may destroy stored data, which is the kind of user-data-impacting behavior that should be disclosed in markdown skill documentation.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning near the example stating that `dropDB` deletes an existing database and may permanently remove data. Recommend using a test-only path, backing up data first, or commenting out the deletion step unless the user intentionally wants cleanup.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8454.md","start_line":280,"end_line":281}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4882257214ef42a982b9a073c68c2352","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_85.md","start_line":14,"end_line":20},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file describes running a local function in parallel on specified nodes or across all data/compute nodes in a cluster, which can affect many systems at once. The description explains behavior but does not provide any caution about cluster-wide impact, unintended execution on all eligible nodes, or the need to verify target nodes before use.","remediation":"Add a user-facing warning near the function description stating that omitting the nodes parameter may execute the function across all eligible cluster nodes and could impact cluster state, performance, or data depending on the invoked function. Recommend verifying node scope before running.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_85.md","start_line":14,"end_line":20}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f6f82d074754435eb64ea3ad001dbec3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8520.md","start_line":29,"end_line":29},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file states that the `script` column contains the exact script string written by the user, and the example later shows full query text and storage paths. Because this is documentation, a user-facing warning is expected when a feature can disclose user-authored queries or internal dataset locations, but no warning is provided.","remediation":"Add a brief warning near the `script` field description or example noting that trace output may contain sensitive SQL text, table names, paths, or business logic, and advise users to avoid sharing trace results from sensitive environments without review.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8520.md","start_line":29,"end_line":29}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-def22774ddec45de9a26f5b9c7b1638d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8552.md","start_line":9,"end_line":64},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains multiple `drop database` and `drop table` commands, which delete databases and tables, but it does not include any warning that these operations are destructive or potentially irreversible. For markdown files, the skill description should warn about behaviors that may affect user data or system integrity.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the first command examples stating that `drop` permanently removes databases/tables, may cause data loss, and should only be run after verifying the target and ensuring backups or recovery plans exist.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8552.md","start_line":9,"end_line":64}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-91212124d73b46b6a707be213848b8c8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8731.md","start_line":13,"end_line":22},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents saving a model to a local server file and explicitly accepts an absolute or relative output path, which can affect server-side data and filesystem state. The description provides no caution about file creation/overwrite behavior or that the write occurs on the server, so users may not realize the operation has system impact.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that saveModel writes to the server filesystem, may overwrite existing files depending on path handling, and should be used only with intended locations and appropriate permissions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8731.md","start_line":13,"end_line":22}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-b4e5c8782ff14bd4a33655d39044d4e0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8753.md","start_line":141,"end_line":150},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that setting initialDB=true deletes the existing database and initialTB=true deletes the existing table, but the surrounding usage guidance does not present this as an explicit caution or warning to users before execution. Because these are irreversible data-destructive actions, the skill description should prominently disclose the risk where parameters are introduced or examples are shown.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning block near the parameter descriptions and usage examples stating that initialDB=true will delete and recreate the target database and initialTB=true will delete and recreate the target table, potentially causing irreversible data loss. Recommend backups and careful validation before enabling either option.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8753.md","start_line":141,"end_line":150}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-51086972d8b4411081f9c7faa310d707","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8753.md","start_line":906,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"b7db67b115bb8e99dfe1f99d0e195ab2adbb5dbdbb6eb6c66ea423ba675152a6","occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_8753.md","start_line":906,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-51086972d8b4411081f9c7faa310d707","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/doc_8753.md","start_line":1419,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the u