":"Add a clear warning near the parameter description stating that calling `unloadVocab()` without `vocabName` removes all loaded vocabularies, and recommend users verify intent before using the no-argument form.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9086.md","start_line":16,"end_line":16}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-4e1a4835e48746508400cb4c9a174a24","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_914.md","start_line":199,"end_line":208},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file contains executable Python example code that connects to DolphinDB using explicit username and password values. The surrounding documentation does not warn readers about credential sensitivity, secret handling, or the risks of reusing hardcoded credentials in real environments.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the example stating that credentials are sensitive and should not be hardcoded in production. Replace literal credentials with placeholders or environment-variable examples, and advise users to use least-privilege accounts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_914.md","start_line":199,"end_line":208}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-ec417e4b53df43f288ca203a16a5b6f0","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/doc_914.md","start_line":216,"end_line":218},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation instructs readers to execute tableInsert against a shared stream table, and elsewhere demonstrates append and table creation/drop operations. The markdown does not clearly warn that running these commands changes server-side state and may overwrite or insert persistent data.","remediation":"Add a user warning before the write operations explaining that the commands modify DolphinD