r identifiers, client IP/port, timestamps, and error details, and that it should only be used by authorized users in appropriate environments.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9166.md","start_line":13,"end_line":48}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6504a805c2c34c09962e3a20eeafed1f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9275.md","start_line":55,"end_line":58},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `nullFill!` as modifying the input object in place, but it does not include any cautionary note about mutating data or the need to avoid unintended overwrites. For markdown files, destructive or data-affecting behavior should be accompanied by a warning when it could impact user data or system integrity.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the description of `nullFill!` stating that it mutates the original object in place and may overwrite existing data. Recommend using `nullFill` instead when users need a non-mutating alternative or want to preserve the original data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9275.md","start_line":55,"end_line":58}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c2c6be7d426144ffa282a9f27b1e56b6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9293.md","start_line":15,"end_line":21},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file explains that `clear!` removes all contents from `X`, which can affect user data and system state, but it does not include any caution about destructive impact or reversibility. Under the markdown-specific warning rule, descriptions of behavior that can alter or erase data should disclose that risk to the user.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the function description stating that `clear!` empties the target object in place and may result in loss of current contents. If applicable, mention that users should back up or confirm they no longer need the data before running it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9293.md","start_line":15,"end_line":21}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-5212e9f292a14b0eae5777954b8a2cad","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":153,"end_line":183},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file states that `closeInactiveSessions` closes all expired sessions, which can disrupt user activity and affect system availability, but it does not provide an explicit cautionary warning. In markdown documentation, actions affecting user sessions or system integrity should disclose that impact clearly.","remediation":"Add a warning that the function forcibly closes inactive sessions across nodes, may interrupt users, and should be run only after verifying the inactivity threshold is appropriate.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":153,"end_line":183}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-28138b32af6a48e7ac3897c5ac9b6627","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":254,"end_line":293},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file documents `dropRecoveringPartitions` as forcibly deleting recovering partitions, but the surrounding description and example do not include a clear safety warning about potential data loss or the irreversible operational impact. For markdown files, destructive behaviors that can affect user data or system integrity should be explicitly warned about.","remediation":"Add a prominent warning near the function description and example stating that `dropRecoveringPartitions` forcibly deletes recovering partitions, may cause permanent data loss, and should only be used after confirming recovery is not needed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":254,"end_line":293}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-23814280b59b468281536a3d86c03b05","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":341,"end_line":352},"finding":null,"explanation":"The function documentation notes that omitting `tbName` cancels all table subscriptions, but it does not clearly warn that this broad action may interrupt streaming consumers and data processing. Because this affects system behavior and can be disruptive, the markdown should include a visible caution.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that calling `unsubscribeAll()` with no argument removes all subscriptions on the node/context and may interrupt dependent streaming jobs.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":341,"end_line":352}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6a9c038c09a14a47904da2ba0c7572f2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":490,"end_line":495},"finding":null,"explanation":"The description states that all stream data engine definitions are released, which is a disruptive and potentially hard-to-recover action, but there is no explicit warning in the markdown. Users should be informed of the operational impact before invoking such a broad destructive function.","remediation":"Add a warning that `dropAllEngines()` removes all stream engine definitions on the current node, may stop active processing, and should be used only after confirming dependencies.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9338.md","start_line":490,"end_line":495}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-62cc7357b70449ffaf4f01b60af1ce35","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/doc_9382.md","start_line":101,"end_line":113},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file includes an example callback that sends job status and results to an external email system and hardcodes an email password in the sample. The surrounding description does not warn users that the example transmits job information externally or that credentials must be handled securely.","remediation":"Add a clear warning near the example that the callback sends job metadata/results to an external service and that users should not hardcode passwords. Recommend using secure secret storage or environment-based credential management instead.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_9382.md","start_line":101,"end_line":113}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-18d880be8d734963a3ea7d227b6fa1df","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/doc_940.md","start_line":34,"end_line":52},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file shows login examples using `-uid admin -pwd 123456` on both Linux and Windows. Exposing credentials on the command line can leak them through shell history or process listings, and the document does not warn users about that risk or advise using safer authentication practices.","remediation":"Add a visible warning near the examples that the shown credentials are placeholders, should not be used in production, and that passing passwords on the command line may expose them via history or process inspection. Recommend prompting for credentials, using a secure secret store, or omitting `-pwd` and logging in interactively where possible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_940.md","start_line":34,"end_line":52}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f61720bdc0e24559a4b1464bb355578c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.87,"location":{"file":"references/doc_940.md","start_line":140,"end_line":156},"finding":null,"explanation":"This section demonstrates reading a local file and inserting its contents into a remote distributed database table via `remoteRun`, which can alter persistent remote data. The markdown explains how to perform the operation but does not include any caution about validating the target database/table, reviewing the input data, or understanding the write impact.","remediation":"Add a warning that the example performs a remote write to persistent database storage, may modify production data, and should be tested against non-production targets first. Advise users to verify connection parameters, target table names, and input file contents before running the command.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/doc_940.md","start_line":140,"end_line":156}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f974ced8132740f1aca169c7ed4481e8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/doc_940.md","start_line":158,"end_line":187},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document explains that `-run` will send a local script file to the remote server and execute it, which can trigger arbitrary actions on the remote database environment. There is no explicit caution about reviewing script contents, using trusted scripts only, or understanding the operational impact before execution.","remediation":"Add a clear warning that `-run` executes the specified local script on the remote server, potentially causing data or system changes. Recommend reviewing script contents, using least-privilege accounts